   "refs": [
    "dave"
   ],
   "key": "Night, a living room lit warm from frame left by a table lamp with a cream shade. Medium close-up of the fat bald plumber with the little tuft of brown hair and the thick brown mustache, facing the camera. He wears a too-tight orange short-sleeve bowling shirt with a black collar and no writing, buttoned up over his blue overalls and white t-shirt, the blue overall bib and one strap showing through the gap between two straining buttons. The collar squeezes his double chin. One small grey smear of pipe grime is on his left cheek, the cheek at frame right. One bead of sweat sits at the top of his bald head. His chin is raised and his eyes are squeezed shut in a wince. His hands are out of frame. Behind his shoulder, soft and out of focus on a beige wall, hangs one big framed photo of a man in the same orange bowling shirt standing next to a white boat, no text. No other people are visible.",
   "move": "slow push-in already moving from the first frame, he says it wincing with his eyes shut, flat and sincere, the bead of sweat stays where it is"
  },
  {
