    "dave"
   ],
   "key": "Night in the same living room. Keep the bowling shirt exactly as in the s01 keyframe. Close-up from a low three-quarter angle from his left side, warm lamp light falling on his face, the lamp itself out of frame. The fat bald plumber with the little tuft of brown hair and the thick brown mustache. He wears a too-tight orange short-sleeve bowling shirt with a black collar and no writing, buttoned up over his blue overalls and white t-shirt; the black collar squeezes his double chin, and at the bottom edge of the frame the blue overall bib shows through the gap between two straining buttons. One small grey smear of pipe grime is on his left cheek, the cheek nearer the camera. One bead of sweat sits at the top of his bald head. His eyes are squeezed shut in a wince and his chin is up. His hands are out of frame. Behind him is a soft beige wall.",
   "move": "he finishes the apology with his eyes shut, wincing, his chin up"
  },
