   "key": "Mid-afternoon in a living room, a window at frame left behind the couch letting in daylight with long warm shadows. A static medium-wide shot. The single focal point is one fat white photo album lying open on the plumber's lap, its pages bright in the window light, with one photo under the woman's fingertip. The fat bald plumber with the thick brown mustache, in blue overalls over a white t-shirt, sits on a floral couch, staring down at the album with heavy-lidded, almost-closed eyes, mouth closed. His hands rest on his thighs beside the album, away from the pages. On his left sits the middle-aged woman with curly red hair in pink foam curlers and big gold hoop earrings, in a mint-green terrycloth bathrobe, her face in profile looking down, mouth closed, her right index finger pressing on one photo in the album on his lap. On the wall behind them hangs one big framed photo of a man in an orange bowling shirt with a black collar standing next to a white boat, his face small and simple, no text. Beside the couch stands an empty side table with a table lamp with a cream shade, switched off. Nothing else on the side table. No clocks."
